NEW_SECTION (line 3)
`Component` (`vUX-component.js`) is bring-your-own-component: you write the markup, mark it with `data-v-*` bindings, and vUX clones, binds, wires and tears down instances of it. It is the module for the reusable pieces of *your* interface (a user card, a board row, a notification) as opposed to the ready-made widgets the rest of the library provides.
REASON
Em dash cleanup (workspace rule: no em dashes in any project). Each U+2014 is rewritten by context: a colon for an explanation or list, a comma before a conjunction (and, but, which...) or when the clause already has a colon, parentheses for a paired aside, a hyphen for an empty value (table cells, placeholders). Sentences the first pass garbled were corrected by hand after two features-validator reviews. No wording or behaviour change otherwise.

OLD_SECTION (line 5)
It is deliberately **not** a framework. There is no observation, no scheduler, no virtual tree and no diffing. A binding is read when an instance is built and again when you call `update()`, and nothing happens in between. What you get is the tedious part [em dash] cloning, field and attribute binding, event wiring, keyed list reconciliation and teardown [em dash] over markup that stays yours.
NEW_SECTION (line 5)
It is deliberately **not** a framework. There is no observation, no scheduler, no virtual tree and no diffing. A binding is read when an instance is built and again when you call `update()`, and nothing happens in between. What you get is the tedious part (cloning, field and attribute binding, event wiring, keyed list reconciliation and teardown) over markup that stays yours.
